\title{picklerick: Fast Single-Cell Format Conversion via SCX}
\description{
R bindings to the SCX streaming interop engine for single-cell genomics. Reads AnnData (.h5ad and Zarr), H5Seurat, 10x HDF5, 10x MatrixMarket and BPCells files into SingleCellExperiment or Seurat objects, or wraps the matrix in a DelayedArray that reads cells on demand. Converts between formats through a memory-bounded streaming pipeline and inspects file metadata without loading the matrix. No Python dependency.
}
\details{
Start with \code{\link[=read_h5ad]{read_h5ad()}} to read a file into a \code{SingleCellExperiment} or
\code{Seurat} object, \code{\link[=inspect]{inspect()}} to look at a file without reading its
matrix, and \code{\link[=convert]{convert()}} to stream one format into another.
\code{vignette("picklerick")} runs each of them on the files shipped in
\code{inst/extdata}.
}
\section{The scx binary}{

The engine is compiled into the package, so no external program is
needed. When the compiled entry points are unavailable, \code{\link[=convert]{convert()}} falls
back to the \code{scx} command-line binary, found in this order:
\enumerate{
\item \code{options(picklerick.scx_binary = "/path/to/scx")}
\item the \code{PICKLERICK_SCX} environment variable
\item \code{scx} on the \code{PATH}
}
}

